"""Create the Step 5 reference and main README updates from executed evidence."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
import pandas as pd
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];ROOT=B.parent

def document(output):
    student=pd.read_csv(output/'student_test_comparison.csv');comp=pd.read_csv(output/'cv_vs_student.csv')
    labels=pd.read_csv(output/'candidate_miss_report.csv');continuity=pd.read_csv(output/'continuity_summary.csv')
    features=pd.read_csv(output/'feature_analysis.csv');selection=json.loads((output/'preliminary_selection.json').read_text())
    meta=json.loads((output/'run_metadata.json').read_text());verified=json.loads((output/'verification.json').read_text())
    suites=list(ET.parse(output/'pytest-results.xml').getroot().iter('testsuite'));tests={k:sum(int(s.get(k,0)) for s in suites) for k in ['tests','failures','errors','skipped']}
    ordered=comp.sort_values(['top1_accuracy','macro_f1','log_loss'],ascending=[False,False,True])
    lines=['# Step 05: detailed evaluation and student-test comparison','',
      '## Objective and completed scope',
      'Evaluate five frozen Step 4 full-training pipelines against qualified student-test references, compare the genuine held-out CV evidence, inspect classifier-only connectivity, and nominate an untuned Step 6 candidate. No model, imputer or scaler was fitted. All model/configuration/source checksums were preserved. Earlier Step 1–4 pipelines were reused; they were not re-executed.', '',
      '## Assignment policy and two-laptop separation',
      'Models and Training Guidelines §4 and Dataset Exploration partition rules explicitly permit ten student-testing trips for development comparison. References enter evaluation only. Evaluator-testing data remains unavailable and untouched. All code/data/model computation stays on Laptop 1. Laptop 2 remains a separate, unimplemented HTTP/Streamlit/Folium client placeholder; no backend dependencies or reference labels were placed there.', '',
      '## Data, frozen labels and execution order',
      '1. Verify the five Step 4 pipeline SHA-256 values and the completed 25-fold verification record. Read the existing 113,639 student-test feature rows. Predict all five models using exactly the ordered 25 inference features before any student-test route file is opened. Prediction cache identity includes the model and feature-file hashes, not routes or labels.',
      '2. Load routes only inside the separate evaluation phase. Reuse Step 3 cleaned observations and the identical alignment implementation/code hash. Radius=75 m, ambiguity margin=2 cost units, heading penalty=20, progress jitter tolerance=5 m, gap threshold=5 s, speed flag=180 km/h, displacement flag=500 m. The frozen ordered-reference dynamic program retains route occurrences/direction/components; safety checks exclude cross-reset order regressions and heading contradictions >90 degrees. No threshold or candidate set was adjusted using student-test results.',
      '3. Join prediction and evaluation labels by partition, original trip, observation and candidate arc IDs. Qualification keeps only valid reference-derived alignments. If a qualified reference arc is absent, retain a candidate miss and null candidate targets; do not manufacture positives or all-negative training examples. These are evaluation targets, never training labels.', '',
      'The alignment uses supplied references and is heuristic, not independently verified physical truth. Its forward/backward path-cost margin is not a calibrated confidence probability. Ambiguous, unmatched and excluded states remain explicit in separate evaluation-only Parquet files.', '',
      '## Actual evaluation coverage','',
      '| Quantity | Count |','|---|---:|',
      *[f'| {column} | {int(labels[column].sum())} |' for column in ['observations','qualified_alignments','candidate_present','candidate_misses','ambiguous','unmatched_alignment','excluded']],
      '',f"Qualification coverage: {labels.qualified_alignments.sum()/labels.observations.sum():.6%}. Candidate miss rate: {labels.candidate_misses.sum()/labels.qualified_alignments.sum():.6%}. Candidate-classification denominator: {int(student.iloc[0].classification_rows)} candidate rows in {int(student.iloc[0].candidate_present_alignments)} qualified candidate-present observation groups. Every model has probability coverage {student.iloc[0].prediction_coverage:.1%} of all {int(student.iloc[0].raw_observations)} raw observations because the original student candidate sets contain no unmatched GPS observation.", '',
      '## Metric definitions and denominators',
      '- Candidate accuracy = (TP+TN)/(TP+TN+FP+FN), on eligible candidate-present groups only; threshold is 0.5.',
      '- Precision = TP/(TP+FP), recall = TP/(TP+FN), binary F1 = 2TP/(2TP+FP+FN), for positive class 1. Undefined precision/recall/F1 denominators use zero, following the explicitly chosen Step 4 convention.',
      '- Macro F1 = mean of positive-class and negative-class F1. It is distinct from binary F1; neither is observation ranking accuracy.',
      '- ROC-AUC uses positive-class scores when both classes exist; otherwise it is undefined/null. Binary log loss = mean[-y log(p) - (1-y) log(1-p)] with sklearn numerical probability clipping.',
      '- Conditional Top-1 = correct highest-probability candidates / qualified reference-present observations. Sort within original trip/observation by probability descending, then original arc ID ascending for ties.',
      '- MRR = mean reciprocal rank of the qualified reference candidate, using the same candidate-present denominator.',
      '- Candidate miss rate = qualified alignments without their reference arc / all qualified alignments. Miss-aware Top-1 = correct Top-1 / all qualified alignments, with each absent reference candidate counting as failure. No accuracy is claimed for unqualified raw observations.',
      '- Prediction coverage = raw observations with a scored candidate / all raw observations, independent of label availability. Evaluation alignment coverage and reference candidate coverage are reported separately.',
      '- Inference milliseconds per observation = 1000 × measured probability-scoring seconds / raw GPS count. Per-trip and total times are retained. Feature I/O, model loading, reference alignment and connectivity computation are excluded from probability-scoring time. This is one measured pass, not an isolated repeated microbenchmark; short times vary with load.', '',
      '## Complete five-model student-test results','',
      '| Model | Accuracy | Precision | Recall | Binary F1 | Macro F1 | ROC-AUC | Conditional Top-1 | Miss-aware Top-1 | MRR | Log loss | ms/GPS |',
      '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for r in ordered.itertuples():lines.append(f'| {r.model_name} | {r.accuracy:.6f} | {r.precision:.6f} | {r.recall:.6f} | {r.f1:.6f} | {r.macro_f1:.6f} | {r.roc_auc:.6f} | {r.top1_accuracy:.6f} | {r.top1_including_candidate_misses:.6f} | {r.mean_reciprocal_rank:.6f} | {r.log_loss:.6f} | {r.inference_ms_per_observation:.6f} |')
    lines += ['', 'All student-test metrics above pool rows or observation groups across the ten trips. per_trip_metrics.csv retains the ten individual trip results for each model. confusion_matrices.png depicts actual pooled candidate counts. Prediction files remain target-free; label files are separate.', '',
      '## Cross-validation versus student-test generalisation','',
      '| Model | CV Macro F1 | Student Macro F1 | CV Top-1 ± fold SD | Student Top-1 | CV log loss | Student log loss |',
      '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for r in ordered.itertuples():lines.append(f'| {r.model_name} | {r.macro_f1_mean:.6f} | {r.macro_f1:.6f} | {r.top1_accuracy_mean:.6f} ± {r.top1_accuracy_std:.6f} | {r.top1_accuracy:.6f} | {r.log_loss_mean:.6f} | {r.log_loss:.6f} |')
    lines += ['',
      'CV values are the unchanged Step 4 equal-weight mean over five held-out trip folds (64 fitting and 16 held-out trips), while student-test values pool ten trips. Both use the same reference-derived eligibility, feature definitions, positive mapping and candidate-present classification/ranking policies. Trip sets, candidate geometry, alignment coverage and aggregation weights differ; the comparison does not isolate distribution shift. CV candidate misses were excluded from the Step 4 OOF denominator, so compare CV Top-1 with conditional student Top-1, not miss-aware Top-1.',
      'Student-test results being higher than CV does not prove absence of overfitting: the student trips and qualified subset may be easier. There are no new training-set scores and therefore no measured training-versus-validation gap in this stage. The fold SDs show substantial variability. The tree’s less favourable log loss than its F1 suggests comparatively poor probability quality; Gaussian NB has the largest student log loss, consistent with potentially overconfident errors under correlated features. These are observations, not causal diagnoses. Limited linear flexibility can explain some differences, but underfitting is not established solely by these tables.', '',
      '## Classifier-only route connectivity',
      'Use original GPS row order, including observations without evaluation labels. Consecutive source observations with elapsed time >5 s are temporal-gap pairs; nonfinite/nonpositive time is invalid. Missing predicted neighbours are recorded and never bridged. Remaining adjacent pairs are the assessable denominator.',
      'Categories are: same original arc; directly connected (previous to-node equals next from-node); intermediate-required (a directed path exists from previous end to next start); unreachable (no directed path). Strongly connected component condensation and cached DAG descendants answer exact topological reachability, without generating routes or calculating HMM transitions. Parallel arcs can collapse in the topology-only graph without changing reachability; original arc IDs remain intact in predictions. Zero-length connectors remain in connectivity.',
      'Direct continuity = (same-arc + directly-connected)/assessable pairs. Reachability = (same-arc + directly-connected + intermediate-required)/assessable pairs. Same-arc fraction decreases are separately flagged; same-arc counts do not certify correct direction or motion. A topological path can be long or implausible for the elapsed time; no path-distance/speed feasibility or reconstruction is claimed.', '',
      '| Partition | Model | Assessable pairs | Direct continuity | Intermediate required | Unreachable | Gap pairs | Missing neighbour pairs | Backward same-arc fractions |',
      '|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for r in continuity.itertuples():lines.append(f'| {r.dataset_partition} | {r.model_name} | {r.assessable_pairs} | {r.direct_continuity:.6f} | {r.intermediate_required} | {r.unreachable} | {r.temporal_gap} | {r.missing_prediction} | {r.same_arc_backward_fraction} |')
    lines += ['',
      'Student continuity uses all raw student observations. CV continuity uses only saved OOF winners for qualified, candidate-present training observations; many raw neighbours lack OOF scores and are excluded. Therefore their direct percentages are descriptive, not comparable population estimates. No CV pipeline was retrained to fill missing predictions. No HMM/Viterbi or reconstructed route exists.', '',
      '## Feature interpretation: actual evidence',
      'Step 4 Logistic Regression standardized coefficients and tree/forest impurity effects were reused. New permutation importance evaluates all 25 inference features on at most 1,000 deterministic evenly spaced qualified observation groups, keeping complete groups, with two shuffles, seed 42 and decrease in candidate Macro F1. Saved models are only scored, never fitted; this is diagnostic interpretation, not feature selection or candidate/label tuning. Full sample row keys, hash identities, timing, means and repeat SDs are retained.', '',
      '| Model | Five largest permutation effects (Macro F1 decrease) |','|---|---|']
    for name,g in features.groupby('model_name'):
        lines.append('| '+name+' | '+'; '.join(f'{r.feature}: {r.importance_mean:.5f}' for r in g.nlargest(5,'importance_mean').itertuples())+' |')
    lines += ['',
      'Heading disagreement and retrieval rank dominate this measured sample across models; distance and segment endpoint positions also contribute. Distance describes geometric proximity; heading disagreement encodes directed compatibility; candidate rank summarizes geometry-based retrieval. Connectivity degrees describe graph branching but do not establish which route was travelled. Gap and quality flags may show small/zero effects because qualified labels exclude many problematic observations and the sample contains few gap cases. That does not establish that temporal gaps are unimportant for future decoding. Correlated features can share importance; shuffling can create inconsistent geometries, and impurity measures favour some feature types. None establishes causation.', '',
      '## Promising model, backup and trade-offs',
      f"Promising untuned model for Step 6: **{selection['promising_model']}**. Backup: **{selection['backup_model']}**. Ranking prioritises student conditional Top-1, then Macro F1 and log loss for exact ties. The observed Top-1 gap is {selection['top1_gap_percentage_points']:.6f} percentage points, not evidence of a statistically significant advantage.",
      'Random Forest narrowly leads student Top-1 and Macro F1 and has slightly higher direct continuity than HGB. HGB remains a strong alternative: better log loss/ROC-AUC/MRR, slightly better CV Top-1 and lower CV fold variability, a smaller saved artifact and slightly lower measured scoring time here. Gaussian NB’s direct continuity is high despite weaker classification/probability results, illustrating why continuity alone cannot select a correct model. All models produce positive-class probabilities compatible with future emission modelling; probabilities are binary candidate scores and are not normalised over a route. Selection remains preliminary and must be revisited after training-trip Bayesian optimisation and proper decoder comparison.', '',
      '## Runtime, complexity and reusable artifacts',
      f"Evaluation pipeline elapsed {meta['runtime_seconds']:.3f} seconds, including ten reference alignments and 90 topology diagnostics, without retraining. Reporting/interpretation elapsed {selection['report_seconds']:.3f} seconds separately. Per-model actual scoring seconds: "+'; '.join(f'{r.model_name}={r.inference_seconds:.6f}' for r in student.itertuples())+'.',
      'Saved artifact byte sizes, CV training/scoring durations and configurations are included in the comparison. File size is a complexity proxy, not a direct RAM/FLOP count. RF has 24 depth-limited trees; HGB has 100 boosting rounds. Timings include one short scoring pass and should not be interpreted as a definitive latency ranking.', '',
      '## Modules and function contracts',
      '- evaluation.predict_frame(pipeline, features) -> identifiers and probabilities only; requires the frozen feature schema and never accepts routes.',
      '- evaluation.evaluation_alignment(network, cleaned, route, configuration) -> identical Step 3 alignment with a frozen-configuration guard; used only in evaluation.',
      '- evaluation.qualify_evaluation(candidates, alignment) -> nullable evaluation targets plus observation eligibility/candidate presence, preserving misses.',
      '- evaluation.score_evaluation(predictions, labels, observation_labels, raw_count) -> pooled candidate, ranking, coverage and miss-aware metrics; rejects mismatched identities.',
      '- evaluation.top1(predictions) -> one deterministic winning candidate per trip/observation.',
      '- continuity.DirectedReachability(nodes, arcs) -> cached directed topology reachability; continuity_diagnostics -> every consecutive source-pair category; summarise_continuity -> counts and denominator-explicit percentages.',
      '- scripts/evaluate_step5.py -> feature-only predictions, separate evaluation references, scoring and CV/student connectivity; caches predictions/labels with input hashes.',
      '- scripts/report_step5.py -> comparisons, plots, read-only permutation diagnostics, preliminary selection; no fitting.',
      '- scripts/verify_step5.py -> complete metric replay, target-free probability replay with Pipeline.fit disabled, source/model hashes, continuity accounting and report/schema checks.',
      '- scripts/document_step5.py -> this reference, summary and all three main README updates from actual evidence.', '',
      '## Tools and outputs',
      'No new dependencies: NumPy/Pandas and PyArrow handle arrays/Parquet, existing Scikit-learn/Joblib pipelines score models, PyProj/Shapely support the reused reference alignment, NetworkX handles directed connectivity, threadpoolctl limits native scoring threads, Matplotlib plots and pytest validates behaviour.',
      'outputs/step5 contains student_test_comparison.csv; cv_vs_student.csv; per_trip_metrics.csv; candidate_miss_report.csv; inference_times.csv; continuity_by_trip.csv and continuity_summary.csv; detailed continuity_pairs/<partition>/<model>/<trip>.parquet; feature_analysis.csv and reused_feature_effects.csv; per-model permutation CSV/identity JSON; interpretability_sample_keys.parquet; preliminary_selection.json; run_metadata.json; verification.json; actual test results; STEP5_SUMMARY.md. Prediction-only Parquet is under predictions/<model>/; evaluation-only alignment and nullable targets are under evaluation_labels/<trip>/. Prior data and model folders are unchanged.',
      'PNG files are top1_comparison.png, macro_f1_comparison.png, log_loss_comparison.png, confusion_matrices.png and permutation_importance.png. These use actual saved results; no learning curves are invented.', '',
      '## Tests and independent verification',json.dumps(tests),json.dumps(verified),
      'Fourteen Step 5 tests cover target-free inference without fitting, model reload, frozen alignment dispatch, candidate misses/ambiguity/undefined conditional scores, identity mismatch, ordering/ties, all continuity categories, gaps/missing neighbours, backward fraction flags and report/pooled-metric consistency. All earlier 101 tests remain intact. Verification replayed every probability for every student model/trip with fitting disabled, recomputed all metrics, checked all 450 model/trip continuity records, compared unchanged CV values, inspected all 125 permutation feature rows and validated PNG files. No earlier expensive pipeline was regenerated.', '',
      '## Exact Windows PowerShell commands','```powershell',
      'cd .\\PathSnap\\laptop1_backend',
      '.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe scripts\\evaluate_step5.py',
      '.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe scripts\\report_step5.py',
      '.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe scripts\\verify_step5.py',
      '.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m pytest -q --junitxml=outputs\\step5\\pytest-results.xml',
      '.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe scripts\\document_step5.py','```',
      'These scripts accept --output. Re-execution reuses prediction/reference/importance caches with matching identities. Source geometry is read for the new continuity analysis, not to rerun EDA/candidate generation. Models are never trained by these commands. Model loading and feature ordering require the existing backend environment.', '',
      '## Limitations, completion and Step 6 readiness',
      'All five models and ten student trips were evaluated; no required stage work remains blocked. Labels remain heuristic and selection-conditioned, student testing is development data, and ten trips give limited evidence about unseen geography. Conditional Top-1 is not accuracy over every raw observation; misses and exclusions have separate denominators. Pooling student data and equal-fold CV weighting differ. Strong graph reachability does not prove plausible route reconstruction. Permutation results use a small deterministic sample and two shuffles; they do not establish causal importance or globally optimal feature choice.',
      'The saved Step 4 pipelines, qualified evaluation-only labels, candidate misses, actual probabilities and reusable topology diagnostics are ready for the separately approved Step 6 optimisation. No optimiser, new model fitting, HMM/Viterbi, FastAPI, Streamlit or deployment ZIP was implemented. Do not tune to evaluator data or claim this untuned choice is final.', '',
      'Changelog — 2026-11-18: Step 5 added separated student prediction/reference evaluation, full metrics and miss accounting, classifier-only directed continuity, feature interpretation, real plots, tests, verification and documentation. AI-assisted implementation and reporting should be reviewed and disclosed under assignment policy.','']
    text='\n\n'.join(lines);(ROOT/'docs/steps/STEP_05_README.md').write_text(text,encoding='utf-8');(output/'STEP5_SUMMARY.md').write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
    for path,prefix in [(ROOT/'README.md','docs/steps/'),(B/'README.md','../docs/steps/'),(ROOT/'laptop2_frontend/README.md','../docs/steps/')]:
        old=path.read_text(encoding='utf-8');marker='\n<!-- STEP5_CURRENT -->'
        if marker in old:old=old.split(marker)[0]
        old=old.replace('**Steps 1–4 are implemented:**','**Steps 1–5 are implemented:**').replace('five baseline models with trip-held-out CV. Detailed evaluation, optimisation,','five baseline models with trip-held-out CV and detailed student-test evaluation. Optimisation,')
        old=old.replace('# Laptop 1: data processing, features and baseline ML (Steps 1–4)','# Laptop 1: data processing, baseline ML and evaluation (Steps 1–5)')
        old=old.replace('Steps 1–4 maintain this directory and documentation only.','Steps 1–5 maintain this directory and documentation only.')
        old=old.replace('- [ ] Step 5 detailed evaluation; not started.','- [x] Step 5 detailed evaluation; see current reference.')
        old=old.replace('## Current status: Step 3 completed','## Historical Step 3 completion record').replace('## Current status: Step 4 completed','## Historical Step 4 completion record')
        old=old.replace('Step 4 baseline ML/CV; stop before Step 5','Step 4 baseline ML/CV → Step 5 detailed evaluation; stop before Step 6')
        old=old.replace('Future approved stages will add defensible GPS/reference alignment and features,\nindependent model comparisons, Bayesian optimisation, HMM/Viterbi, API/UI,\nintegration, deployment and the technical report.',
            'Future approved stages will add Bayesian optimisation, HMM/Viterbi, API/UI, integration, deployment and the technical report. Alignment, baseline models and detailed student-test evaluation are already implemented.')
        old=old.replace('- [ ] Later models, optimisation, route reconstruction, API/UI and deployment.',
            '- [x] Steps 4–5: five baseline models, CV and detailed student-test evaluation.\n- [ ] Later optimisation, route reconstruction, API/UI and deployment.')
        old=old.replace('- [ ] Later models, optimisation, HMM/Viterbi, API/UI, integration, packages/report.',
            '- [x] Steps 4–5: baseline models and detailed evaluation.\n- [ ] Later optimisation, HMM/Viterbi, API/UI, integration, packages/report.')
        old=old.replace('Steps 1–2 are complete; Step 3 requires explicit approval.','Steps 1–5 are complete; Step 6 requires explicit approval.')
        old=old.replace('# Empty; no trained models','# Five saved Step 4 baseline pipelines')
        appendix=marker+f"\n\n## Current status: Step 5 completed\n\n[Step 5 detailed reference]({prefix}STEP_05_README.md). Earlier stage boundaries above are historical. All five saved Step 4 pipelines were evaluated without refitting on 113,639 candidate rows / 19,160 student-test observations. There are 15,121 qualified alignments, 14,547 reference-present groups and 574 candidate misses. Reference labels are evaluation-only and remain separate from predictions and Step 3 training data.\n\nPromising untuned Step 6 model: **{selection['promising_model']}**; backup **{selection['backup_model']}**. The difference is small; see actual Macro F1, Top-1, log loss, CV variability, continuity and timing in the stage reference. Evaluation outputs are in laptop1_backend/outputs/step5/. {tests['tests']} tests, {tests['failures']} failures, {tests['errors']} errors, {tests['skipped']} skipped. No dependencies changed.\n\n- [x] Step 5 evaluation/verification/plots/documentation.\n- [ ] Step 6 Bayesian optimisation: not started. Decoder, API/UI and deployment remain pending. Laptop 2 remains an unimplemented HTTP UI placeholder and contains no reference labels/models/backend dependencies.\n\nChangelog — 2026-11-18: completed Step 5 using frozen Step 3 alignment and Step 4 models/OOF evidence; added reusable evaluation/continuity modules, scripts, tests, plots and reference. No models were trained. Step 6 requires explicit approval.\n"
        path.write_text(old+appendix,encoding='utf-8')
    print('Step 5 summary, separate reference and all three main READMEs updated.')

if __name__=='__main__':
    import argparse
    p=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__);p.add_argument('--output',type=Path,default=B/'outputs/step5');a=p.parse_args();document(a.output)
